    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **23 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince the value is fully derived from the owner's own fields, I followed the same pattern already used for the other read-only derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than adding a persisted column:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression computing the value:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   The `%02d` zero-pads years like 2007 \u2192 `07`, and `year % 100` yields the same two digits the spec/test derive via `registrationDate.substring(2, 4)`.\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests` (membership number format) passes, along with all existing tests including `Cp09Tests` (customerCode) and `Cp07Tests` (registrationDate), which it depends on.",
